[Predictions]

@Miguelpicks if mma math was accurate then we’d all have 100% pick rates. No doubt Perez is losing to killers but he’s got a massive reach disparity to get past and I don’t think Su’s grappling is as bad as it seems. If we really want to cherry pick, the Smolka loss was his debut and the Schnell loss was an all time fumble. Su has clearly improved since then and he is a very tricky puzzle to outpoint on the feet. Perez has been fighting mostly counter strikers or grapplers, now he’s facing the lankiest striker in the divsiob with a 25 hour flight on top of it.

I do think Su gasses but you’ve gotta factor in that he didn’t manage his cardio well. Perez is not some crazy brawler and I don’t think he can just blitz the pocket here because of Su’s size. I think Perez’s striking has looked a lot better than it is because of who he’s fought

